# Firebase CLI deploy cache — local, regenerated on every deploy.
.firebase/

# Vercel CLI link + pulled env. Deploys run from the repository root (see
# .vercelignore), so this lands here as well as in site/. Never commit it:
# `vercel pull` writes .env.production.local into it.
/.vercel
services/market-data/node_modules/
services/market-data/dist/

# ── PRIVATE KEYS. NEVER. ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `python -m py_vapid --gen` writes private_key.pem and public_key.pem into
# the CURRENT DIRECTORY, and the natural place to run it from is the repository
# root. The private half is a credential: whoever holds it can make a
# notification appear that looks like it came from Radar (see the note at the
# top of worker/radar_alerts/send.py).
#
# Generating outside the repository is still the right habit. This is the net
# under it, not a substitute for it.
*.pem
*.p8
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
# The Play upload key's config — RELEASE.md §1. Holds a store password.
android/key.properties
